From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kim Hansen <github@kimhansen.dk>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:14:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Server-side copy: FSCTL_SRV_REQUEST_RESUME_KEY and
 FSCTL_SRV_COPYCHUNK

Session.copyFile(from:to:destinationSession:limits:progressHandler:) asks
the server for the source's resume key and copies it in copy-chunk
requests, so no file data crosses the network. The first request stays
within the limits Windows and Samba both advertise; a server that answers
STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER with its own SRV_COPYCHUNK_RESPONSE limits gets
requests sized to those, once. The destination is created, never
replaced, and deleted again if the copy fails or is cancelled.

SMBClient.copyFile(from:to:share:) copies into another share through a
second tree on the same session; the server decides whether it allows
that. ErrorResponse keeps the whole reply so the limits survive a
non-success status.
